BUG FOUND in the interrupted attempt's extension: the --token=absent run failed
with "Setup's token TextInput not found in the rendered tree" -- not with the
packet's expected RED ("Chat reached with header shown"). Root cause: Fabric's
fake UI manager's createNode(tag, viewName, rootTag, props, instanceHandle)
receives `props.onChange`/`props.onClick` as the boolean `true` (native is only
told "a listener is registered"), never as the JS function -- confirmed against
node_modules/react-native's real behaviour by instrumenting a throwaway copy of
the script (deleted before finishing; not part of the diff) and printing prop
types on the committed TextInput/TouchableOpacity host nodes. The interrupted
attempt's collectTree()/driveToChat code assumed `typeof node.props.onClick ===
"function"` and called it directly, which can never match. The correct
mechanism (already used two lines above in this same file for
RNCSafeAreaProvider's `topInsetsChange`) is to dispatch the native event by
tag/instanceHandle through the fake UI manager's registerEventHandler callback:
`topChange` (RCTTextInputViewConfig's bubblingEventTypes -> TextInput's
`_onChange` reads `nativeEvent.text`/`.eventCount`) for typing, and `topClick`
(View's base config bubblingEventTypes -> Pressability's onClick -> onPress)
for the tap. Fixed in mobile/scripts/runtime-smoke.mjs:
  - createNode now stores `instanceHandle` on the returned fake node so it can
    be dispatched to later.
  - collectTree()'s pressable/text-input detection now keys off
    `props.onClick === true` / `props.onChange === true` (not `typeof ... ===
    "function"`), grouping pressables by node identity instead of function
    identity (which was never unique when onClick was always the same
    boolean).
  - the drive-to-chat block dispatches `topChange` on the token TextInput's
    instanceHandle, then `topClick` on the Continue button's instanceHandle,
    via `dispatchFabricEvent`, instead of calling `.props.onChange(...)` /
    `.onClick(...)` as functions.
  - the module doc comment was corrected to describe event dispatch rather
    than direct handler calls.

