Both RootLayout gating removal effects confirmed: chat/settings/setup are now
declared unconditionally, so after setup.tsx's router.replace("/chat") the
Chat screen's headerShown:false option applies (single top bar,
singleTopBar=true) -- fixing the finding B defect exactly as diagnosed.

What this proves: RootLayout no longer needs a live token read to decide which
screens exist; the same Stack.Screen options apply regardless of navigation
path (fresh launch with token vs. Setup -> replace("/chat") vs., by the same
logic, Chat/Settings -> replace("/setup") after logout). What it does NOT
prove: keyboard geometry on a physical device (KeyboardAvoidingView's
keyboardVerticalOffset={0} correctness given the now-single, hidden Stack
header) -- that requires the human's on-phone check, not provable in this
fake-renderer harness.

